                        "review": "I was an early alpha tester for this game. The game was riddled with issues and the dev would ignore our feedback (or maybe just didn’t have the means to fix these issues). Then all of a sudden he just went ahead and released the game after a very short dev time, and it shows.\n\nWhere should I even begin with all the issues? 1.) I’ve seen better menus/text/UI from flash games from the early 2000s. 2.)  I don’t really mind bad graphics, but these are like PS1 graphics in 2019, this wasn’t some artistic choice, just very bad. Textures don’t even load properly in the second half of the game. 3.) The animations in the game run VERY slowly. There’s a “puzzle” where you move a mine-cart back and forth several times very slowly. It will drive you insane. Sometimes animations don’t happen if you click too fast and you need to leave the area and come back to reset the puzzle. 4.) Puzzle design is horrible, especially in the second half of the game. No one can finish it without a guide because the puzzles are such that unless you designed them, you can’t figure them out. They have really unfair variables thrown in with no way for you to know even after plenty of experimentation.\n\nSeems like no real effort or money went into this. Should have cooked in the oven longer but the dev was eager to release. The game is not worth even a penny sadly.",
